at the result is kind  of pre uh  pre-arranged i think we know that  there's very little chance of anything  but a huge majority for during russia i  think the reason why this is happening  now is partly internal it's because  russia is having huge difficulties  recruiting enough people to fight and if  the russian authorities can claim at  least internally that this is about  ukraine attacking russian territory at  least territory that russia claims  russian territory then it can mobilize  it can force people to fight to  previously be able to get out of  fighting  it's also about trying to kind of bank  some territory and situation where it  looks to be losing ground here in  ukraine showing russian domestic kind of  viewers what this is all about what the  point of this war has been but also more  internationally it's about having the  opportunity to threaten ukraine with the  use potentially of nuclear weapons to  say this is russian territory if you're  going to attack us here then we will use  everything we've got to defend our own  territory now i don't think anyone  outside russia is going to go anywhere  near this and recognise this but that  certainly is the kind of brinkmanship  that seems to be coming into this russia  seemingly convinced that the outside  world especially europe is not willing  to escalate further that it has the kind  of greater tolerance the greater  willingness to go big and to kind of up  the stakes here and hope that somehow  these kind of announcements uh force the  eu european backers and american backers  of ukraine to come back to the table to  negotiating table and maybe call some  kind of truce  how are ukrainian authorities likely to  respond  i think they're going to ignore it we've  seen how the ukraine's army has been  targeting russian military installations  in crimea another part of ukraine that  russia claims is its own territory has  claimed as russian since 2014 and we've  seen consistently announcements from the  us that they  continue to see  crimea as ukraine as such the ban on  using u.s made weapons against russian  territory doesn't apply to crimea it  won't apply to and the hands can so  basically ukraine will continue its  military offensives maybe even trying to  speed things up a bit to get in the way  of this kind of creeping russian  takeover in donetsk and hans  nick connolly for us in hakib thank you  and for an overview of the fast-moving  situation on the ground here's dw  reporter joel dalroy  in a matter of days ukrainian troops  have managed to roll back months worth  of russian gains and although they have  slowed a little they are not stopping as  they push further east well here's a  look at how the military map has changed  at the start of the summer in june  russian forces were in charge of almost  all of the territory from hakeev in the  north to herson in the south but in  early september ukraine launched its  surprise counter-offensive operation in  kharkiv and this is the result they  reclaimed almost all of the hakiv region  there in the north reaching the russian  border and on monday they announced that  they had crossed the oskil river now  that puts ukrainian troops on the  doorstep of neighboring lukansk region  now that is an area that moscow named as  one of its intended targets of its  invasion and ukrainian units are now  moving towards several strategic cities  that they lost to russian troops just  months ago  but these new territorial gains they  come with grisly discoveries near the  city of israel officials are uncovering  a mass grave they estimate over 400  civilians and soldiers were buried there  in recent months some appearing to have  been tortured and it is the second such  mass grave uncovered following russian  occupation the first was near butcher  near kiev where more than 450 bodies  were found  and there are also fears of what might  be found in mariupol in the south that  is still under russian occupation  satellite images appear to show mass  burial sites there too  well russia denies it has carried out  any atrocities or war crimes inspectors  from the united nations are heading to  israel to reach their own conclusions  so as ukrainian troops hope to take more  towns from russia there are fears of  what they may find when they arrive
 

